     "explanation": "The little-bets strategy is Newport's alternative to top-down mission planning. Because the adjacent possible is only visible from the current frontier of accumulated capital, a mission cannot be reasoned out in advance from a distance — it has to be discovered through a series of small, low-cost, fast-feedback experiments conducted at the edge of a field.",
